{
  "scope": "Four sequential isolated server-only gperftools diagnostics with a quiet negotiated CBOR client. Zero/256 incomplete HTTP peers,32 paced one-byte rounds, drained Linux TCP receive queues after each round. Partial metadata stays live until absolute five-second handshake timeout;16 renewed raw slots and later healthy traffic/Close/EOF independently verify retirement and usability. Timings/RSS use a replacement allocator and are excluded from ordinary comparisons. Delta includes fixed management/dump overhead; zero-peer control distinguishes those allocations. Requested object/byte counts, not RSS or a general zero-allocation claim.",
